<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Serilog on Antoine Boucher</title><link>https://antoineboucher.info/CV/blog/tags/serilog/</link><description>Recent content in Serilog on Antoine Boucher</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:00:00 -0400</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://antoineboucher.info/CV/blog/tags/serilog/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Serilog.Sinks.SentrySDK: connecting structured logs to error reporting</title><link>https://antoineboucher.info/CV/blog/posts/serilog-sentrysdk-structured-errors/</link><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:00:00 -0400</pubDate><guid>https://antoineboucher.info/CV/blog/posts/serilog-sentrysdk-structured-errors/</guid><description>&lt;aside class="repo-snapshot" aria-label="GitHub"&gt;
 &lt;a href="https://github.com/antoinebou12/Serilog.Sinks.SentrySDK"&gt;antoinebou12/Serilog.Sinks.SentrySDK&lt;/a&gt;
 &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;★ 2&lt;/strong&gt; · 0 forks · Repository created &lt;time datetime="2023-06-05"&gt;2023-06-05&lt;/time&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
 &lt;small&gt;GitHub statistics recorded &lt;time datetime="2026-10-20"&gt;2026-10-20&lt;/time&gt;.&lt;/small&gt;
&lt;/aside&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A log line tells you that something happened. An error event becomes useful when it also carries the exception, release, environment, and request context needed to investigate it. &lt;strong&gt;Serilog.Sinks.SentrySDK&lt;/strong&gt; connects those two views.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://antoineboucher.info/CV/blog/posts/serilog-sentrysdk-structured-errors/images/featured.png" alt="Serilog Sentry SDK package artwork from src/assets in the repository"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This project is based on &lt;strong&gt;serilog-contrib/serilog-sinks-sentry&lt;/strong&gt;. Its own GitHub stars measure interest in this repository, not total Serilog or Sentry adoption.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Serilog.Sinks.SentrySDK</title><link>https://antoineboucher.info/CV/blog/projects/serilog.sinks.sentrysdk/</link><pubDate>Mon, 06 Sep 2021 22:42:23 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://antoineboucher.info/CV/blog/projects/serilog.sinks.sentrysdk/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="serilogsinkssentrysdk"&gt;Serilog.Sinks.SentrySDK&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A Serilog sink that sends events to Sentry through the official Sentry SDK.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Based on &lt;a href="https://github.com/serilog-contrib/serilog-sinks-sentry"&gt;serilog-contrib/serilog-sinks-sentry&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="project-status"&gt;Project Status&lt;/h2&gt;
